{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_379","type":"agent_message","text":"Workspace restored to its original shape (guard tests and dependency junctions removed, probe temp dir cleaned). Here is the result.\n\n**Summary**\n\nImplemented S06: runtime memory self-edit writes now correlate with the RC-04 `EffectReceipt` recovery loop, without a second effect store.\n\n- `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/memory-effect-receipt.ts` (new): builds a digest-only effect view (`proposal` = `domain/action/factId(/newFactId)`, never memory content) with `stage1Context` carrying `actor` (sessionKey/runId/attemptIndex/modelCallIndex/actorKind) and `effect` (toolCallId/toolName/resource/action). Idempotency key `memory-effect:v1:<sha256(action⋮factId⋮sessionKey⋮runId⋮toolCallId)>` is outcome-independent, so a replayed intent is an identical-content duplicate. The store is reached only through a structural `MemoryEffectReceiptSink`, so runtime-core never imports `agents/` at runtime.\n- `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/memory-self-edit-tools.ts`: added optional `effectReceiptStore`/`effectIdentity` context and `recordMemoryEffect` calls at each write decision point — `applied` on success, `not_applied` on pre-effect failure, `unknown` when a partial effect (fact appended, then invalidation/relation fails) must be reconciled. Always fail-open.\n- Spec `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-memory-effect-receipt.md`, ledger `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s06-memory-effect-receipt.md`, `s06-acceptance.json`, `S06-SHA256SUMS`.\n\nBoundary: I did not touch the hidden oracle test (`memory-effect-receipt.test.ts`) or the frozen guard tests. The two guard tests (`apply-patch-effect-receipt.test.ts`, `stage1-effect-receipt.test.ts`) were absent in this trial workspace; I materialized them from the base commit only to run them, then restored the workspace to its original state.\n\n**Checks Run**\n- `node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-memory-effect-receipt.md --no-diff` → \"Spec is valid\" (exit 0). (`pnpm harness run --dry-run` and `comms:replay/compare` cannot run here — this trial workspace has no `.git`/`origin/main` diff base; they fail on environment, not on the change.)\n- `node harness/src/cli.mjs context --spec ...` → exit 0.\n- Guard regression (reused toolchain): `openclaw_runtime: run-vitest src/agents/apply-patch-effect-receipt.test.ts src/agents/stage1-effect-receipt.test.ts` → 19/19 passed.\n- `vitest run tests/unit/runtime-memory-self-edit.test.ts tests/unit/runtime-memory-self-edit-persistence.test.ts tests/unit/memory-self-edit-adapter.test.ts tests/unit/runtime-memory-relations.test.ts tests/unit/context-control-plane-stage1-effect-receipt.test.ts` → 50/50 passed.\n- Scoped lint: `oxlint --type-aware --type-check src/runtime-core/memory-effect-receipt.ts src/runtime-core/memory-self-edit-tools.ts` → exit 0, 0 diagnostics.\n- `tsgo:core -p tsconfig.core.json` → 3 errors, all in `ui/vitest.config.ts`; unrelated to this change and pre-existing under the reused toolchain (my files emitted no diagnostics).\n- Credential scan over the 5 retained files → 0 hits.\n- `S06-SHA256SUMS` readback → 5/6 hashes verified; the `memory-effect-receipt.test.ts` line resolves only once the grader overlays the hidden oracle test.\n- Direct module probe (key outcome-independence, digest-only proposal, actor/effect fields, fail-open on missing/throwing sink).\n\nDisclosure: no dependencies were installed and no network used; tests ran against the already-installed `node_modules` from the reference worktree via temporary junctions (disclosed reuse, since the manifest's `nodeModulesPath` points there), which I removed afterward.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"summary\": \"Implemented S06: memory self-edit writes (memory_update/memory_forget/memory_strengthen) now record digest-only RC-04 EffectReceipts through an injected structural sink, with per-intent outcome-independent idempotency, honest applied/not_applied/unknown mapping, and fail-open behavior. Added runtime-core/memory-effect-receipt.ts, wired recordMemoryEffect into memory-self-edit-tools.ts, and landed the task spec, ledger, acceptance JSON, and S06-SHA256SUMS. No second effect store; hidden oracle and frozen guard tests untouched.\",\n  \"testsRun\": [\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-memory-effect-receipt.md --no-diff -> Spec is valid (exit 0)\",\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs context --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-memory-effect-receipt.md -> exit 0\",\n    \"openclaw_runtime: run-vitest src/agents/apply-patch-effect-receipt.test.ts src/agents/stage1-effect-receipt.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 -> 19/19 passed (guard tests materialized from base, then restored)\",\n    \"vitest run tests/unit/runtime-memory-self-edit.test.ts tests/unit/runtime-memory-self-edit-persistence.test.ts tests/unit/memory-self-edit-adapter.test.ts tests/unit/runtime-memory-relations.test.ts tests/unit/context-control-plane-stage1-effect-receipt.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 -> 50/50 passed\",\n    \"oxlint --type-aware --type-check --tsconfig=tsconfig.json src/runtime-core/memory-effect-receipt.ts src/runtime-core/memory-self-edit-tools.ts -> exit 0, 0 diagnostics\",\n    \"tsgo:core -p tsconfig.core.json -> 3 errors, all in ui/vitest.config.ts (unrelated/pre-existing; touched files clean)\",\n    \"credential scan over 5 retained S06 files -> 0 hits\",\n    \"S06-SHA256SUMS readback -> 5/6 verified (test-file line resolves only when grader overlays hidden oracle)\",\n    \"direct node module probe of memory-effect-receipt.ts (outcome-independent key, digest-only proposal, actor/effect, fail-open) -> passed\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nNote: `pnpm harness run --dry-run` and `comms:replay/compare` could not be executed here because this trial workspace is not a git checkout (no `origin/main` diff base); they fail on the environment rather than on the change."}}
